  "question": {
    "text": "Two blocks of the same metal having same mass and at\r\n\r\ntemperature $\\mathrm{T}_{1},$ and $\\mathrm{T}_{2}$, respectively, are brought in contact with each other and allowed to attain thermal equilibrium\r\n\r\nat constant pressure. The change in entropy, $\\Delta \\mathrm{S}$, for this\r\n\r\nprocess is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{P}} \\ln \\left[\\frac{\\left(\\mathrm{T}_{1}+\\mathrm{T}_{2}\\right)^{2}}{4 \\mathrm{~T}_{1} \\mathrm{~T}_{2}}\\right]$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$2 C_{p} \\ln \\left[\\frac{\\left(T_{1}+T_{2}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{2}}}{T_{1} T_{2}}\\right]$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$2 \\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{P}} \\ln \\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{T}_{1}+\\mathrm{T}_{2}}{4 \\mathrm{~T}_{1} \\mathrm{~T}_{2}}\\right)$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$2 \\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{P}} \\ln \\left[\\frac{\\mathrm{T}_{1}+\\mathrm{T}_{2}}{2 \\mathrm{~T}_{1} \\mathrm{~T}_{2}}\\right]$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Final temperature $=\\frac{\\mathrm{T}_{1}+\\mathrm{T}_{2}}{2},$ let $\\mathrm{T}_{2}>\\mathrm{T}$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{dS}=\\frac{\\mathrm{dq}}{\\mathrm{T}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{p}} \\mathrm{dT}}{\\mathrm{T}}$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore \\Delta \\mathrm{S}=\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{p}} \\ln \\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{f}}}{\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{i}}}\\right)$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore \\Delta \\mathrm{S}_{\\text {Total }}=\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{p}} \\ln \\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{T}_{1}+\\mathrm{T}_{2}}{2 \\mathrm{~T}_{1}}\\right)+\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{p}} \\ln \\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{T}_{1}+\\mathrm{T}_{2}}{2 \\mathrm{~T}_{2}}\\right)$\r\n\r\n$\\quad=\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{p}} \\ln \\left[\\frac{\\left(\\mathrm{T}_{1}+\\mathrm{T}_{2}\\right)^{2}}{4 \\mathrm{~T}_{1} \\mathrm{~T}_{2}}\\right]$"
  }
}